      "body": "> I think the PR description needs to be updated to clarify that this is only a \"regression\" for macOS/Windows builds. The point of #35537 was to split the Linux builds, and they wont be re-usable going forward.\r\n\r\nThe PR description has been updated.\r\n\r\nRebuilding packages in depends when switching branches is still a regression, even for Linux hosts. This affects all Guix builders, similar to the issue resolved in https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34228.\r\n\r\n> Will this still work if/when we move to static linux builds?\r\n\r\nYes. For the case I mentioned above.",
